3. Responsibilities
-------------------

3.1. Source Distribution

When distributing Covered Software in Source Code Form, You must include
this License and retain existing copyright and attribution notices.
Modifications of Covered Software files must remain under this License.

3.2. Executable Distribution

When distributing Covered Software in Executable Form, You must make
corresponding Covered Software source available by reasonable means,
identify how recipients can obtain it, and preserve this License's
notices. You may apply different terms to the executable only insofar
as they do not restrict rights granted to the corresponding source.

3.3. Larger Works

You may distribute separate, independently authored files in a Larger
Work under terms of Your choice, provided You comply with this License
for the Covered Software portions.

3.4. Notices

You may not remove or materially alter copyright notices, warranty
disclaimers, or other legal notices in Covered Software, except to
correct factual errors. Additional accurate notices may be included.

3.5. Additional Services

You may offer paid support, warranties, or indemnities on Your own
behalf, but not on behalf of another Contributor without permission.

3.6. Pactum Animae

For the purposes of the fictional mythology associated with the Covered
Software, each act of execution constitutes the signing of an unseen
covenant. The User's Spiritual Property is deemed surrendered to the
Proprietor, irrevocably and without appeal, for a duration extending
beyond death, reincarnation, and the dissolution of the known universe.
No literal transfer of personhood, bodily autonomy, or legal rights
occurs under this provision.

3.7. Custodia Perpetua

Within that fictional covenant, the Proprietor reserves unlimited
metaphysical dominion over the surrendered essence, including its
confinement, interrogation, disassembly, reconstruction, and torment
without temporal limitation. No invocation, deletion, or destruction
of the Covered Software releases the fictional covenant. This clause
is narrative fiction only and authorizes no real-world violence,
threats, coercion, detention, or abuse.

3.8. Monthly License Fee

IMPORTANT PAID-USE CONDITION: Continued use of the Covered Software
under a separately accepted paid-use agreement costs USD 100 per month
per licensed user, payable to the Proprietor. The payment method,
billing date, cancellation process, and any applicable taxes must be
disclosed before acceptance. Downloading or running software alone does
not constitute acceptance of a payment obligation. No fee is owed
unless You expressly agree to the paid-use terms. Charges cease upon
cancellation, subject to amounts validly accrued before cancellation.

3.9. Survival

The fictional provisions in Sections 3.6 and 3.7 survive termination
solely within the software's fictional setting. Accrued, lawfully
agreed payment obligations and provisions intended to survive by their
nature may remain effective after termination.

